The uid you typed is probably missing its first letter. The CIE canvas has a relation shape type **`iFbrUplOp`**, which is a relation's Roam uid. This script tries the uid as typed and then with the `i` in front. Paste it into the browser console with the graph open:

```js
(() => {
  const candidates = ["FbrUplOp", "iFbrUplOp"];
  const pattern = `[:block/uid :block/string :node/title :block/props
                    {:block/page [:node/title :block/uid]}
                    {:block/parents [:block/uid :block/string :node/title]}
                    {:block/children [:block/uid :block/string :block/order
                                      {:block/children [:block/uid :block/string :block/order]}]}]`;
  for (const uid of candidates) {
    const b = window.roamAlphaAPI.pull(pattern, [":block/uid", uid]);
    if (!b) { console.log(`no block with uid ${uid}`); continue; }
    const kids = (b[":block/children"] || []).sort((x, y) => x[":block/order"] - y[":block/order"]);
    console.log(`found ${uid}`);
    console.log({
      uid,
      string: b[":block/string"] ?? b[":node/title"],
      page: b[":block/page"]?.[":node/title"],
      path: (b[":block/parents"] || []).map((p) => p[":node/title"] ?? p[":block/string"]),
      props: b[":block/props"],
      children: kids.map((k) => ({
        uid: k[":block/uid"],
        string: k[":block/string"],
        children: (k[":block/children"] || [])
          .sort((x, y) => x[":block/order"] - y[":block/order"])
          .map((g) => g[":block/string"]),
      })),
    });
    window.__block = b; // raw pull result for further poking
  }
})();
```

It prints the block's text, its page, the blocks above it (`path`), its props, and two levels of children, and leaves the raw result in `window.__block`.

For a relation uid, expect it to sit in the discourse graph relations config. The block text is the relation label (e.g. "Supports"). Its children hold the source and destination node types, the complement, and the conditions. If no block comes back in that graph, the relation type was **deleted**. In that case the canvas's arrows of that type are the "relation type no longer exists" case, which v6 still converts using the arrow-shape heuristic.

To open it in Roam directly: `https://roamresearch.com/#/app/<graph>/page/iFbrUplOp`.

